TITLE:: PianoRollLoopMarkers
SUMMARY:: Vertical loop start and stop lines on a piano roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollTimeline

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollLoopMarkers:: holds two LINK::Classes/View:: instances (one beat wide). LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#-stopRecording:: applies the recorded note range by calling LINK::#-setLoopStartFromClickBeat_:: and LINK::#-setLoopEndFromClickBeat_:: in that order (same snapping and ordering rules as timeline clicks). The LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: passed to LINK::#-new:: is only used for the marker colour (LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5::) when the lines are first created.

Snap resolution for timeline clicks is stored in the instance variable CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats:: (beats between snap grid points; default one sixteenth note). Clicks are snapped with rounding before the start/end ordering rules are applied.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollLoopMarkers::. The line LINK::Classes/View::s are created on the first successful call to LINK::#-setLoopStartFromClickBeat_:: or LINK::#-setLoopEndFromClickBeat_::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The roll surface (typically the piano roll LINK::Classes/UserView::) on which the lines are parented.

ARGUMENT:: horizontalScale
Pixels per beat, matching the roll's horizontal scale.

ARGUMENT:: rollHeight
Height of the lines in pixels (typically the full roll height).

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette::; only LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5:: is kept for drawing the lines.

ARGUMENT:: defaultStopBeat
Initial loop end beat before any marker is set (for example the roll length in beats). Pass nil to use a built-in default.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: setLoopStartFromClickBeat_
Snaps the given beat using CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats::, then sets the start marker if the snapped beat is strictly before the current end marker. Otherwise posts a warning and does nothing. Also used when LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: applies the recorded range after LINK::#-stopRecording::.

ARGUMENT:: rawBeat
Unsnapped beat position (e.g. from a timeline click or from recorded note timing).

METHOD:: setLoopEndFromClickBeat_
Snaps the given beat using CODE::prSnapResolutionBeats::, then sets the end marker if the snapped beat is strictly after the current start marker. Otherwise posts a warning and does nothing. Also used when LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: applies the recorded range after LINK::#-stopRecording::.

ARGUMENT:: rawBeat
Unsnapped beat position (e.g. from a timeline click or from recorded note timing).

PRIVATE:: init, prSnapBeat, prUpdateLineViews
